              "cleanup": "Remove destroys its Render node before discarding projected-visual ownership and any matching valid mirror; load and teardown release every tracked Scene Tree-projected node, retain failed elementId cleanup ownership, and discard each still-valid matching entry only after release succeeds.",
              "memoryBound": "At stable boundaries there is at most one entry and one live Scene Tree-projected Render node per live non-workspace Scene Tree element, with no retained removed-node map; custom and overlay layer nodes stay under their own lifecycle owners."
